; Stage 15 W8 G-5, step 4 — the flip (design/global-init.md §5 G-5, acceptance
; criterion (B); closes design/stage15-stress-test/nullability.md §1.5's
; remaining half). A global whose declared type is a NON-NULL typed pointer may
; no longer be left uninitialized: the slot would take type-zero-const-ir's
; `null`, i.e. exactly the value the type promises it can never hold.
;
; Every other position in the language has refused this since Phase F. The
; global declaration was the last hole, and it was only tolerable while there
; was no way to write the initializer at all (G-1/G-2/G-3 supplied one).
(defstruct Thing v:i32)

(defvar g5-thing:ptr:Thing)

(defn main ():i32
  (return (g5-thing v)))
